From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivo Nunes <ivo@nunes.uk>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tvOS: keep user data in Caches, where apps can write

OS_AppleEmbedded::get_user_data_dir() returns the app's Documents
folder on every Apple embedded platform, but tvOS doesn't let apps
write there, so user:// failed on Apple TV: settings, saves and log
files were never written. On tvOS it now returns the Caches folder, the
one place tvOS apps can write. The system may clear it when it needs
space, so data that must last belongs in iCloud or NSUserDefaults
(Purr keeps saves with no copy elsewhere in NSUserDefaults).

Test: on Apple TV, a game writes a file to user:// and reads it back;
the log file appears under Library/Caches/logs.

Upstream: to propose (Godot's tvOS platform is Purr's patch 0007, so
with it).
---
diff --git a/godot/drivers/apple_embedded/os_apple_embedded.mm b/godot/drivers/apple_embedded/os_apple_embedded.mm
index f948d56..df8894a 100644
--- a/godot/drivers/apple_embedded/os_apple_embedded.mm
+++ b/godot/drivers/apple_embedded/os_apple_embedded.mm
@@ -398,7 +398,13 @@ Rect2 fit_keep_aspect_covered(const Vector2 &p_container, const Vector2 &p_rect)
 String OS_AppleEmbedded::get_user_data_dir(const String &p_user_dir) const {
 	static String ret;
 	if (ret.is_empty()) {
+#ifdef TVOS_ENABLED
+		// tvOS apps can't write to their Documents folder: Caches is the one they can (the system
+		// may clear it when it needs space, so data that must last belongs in iCloud or NSUserDefaults).
+		NSArray *paths = NSSearchPathForDirectoriesInDomains(NSCachesDirectory, NSUserDomainMask, YES);
+#else
 		NSArray *paths = NSSearchPathForDirectoriesInDomains(NSDocumentDirectory, NSUserDomainMask, YES);
+#endif
 		if (paths && [paths count] >= 1) {
 			ret.append_utf8([[paths firstObject] UTF8String]);
 		}
